# Local Harness

- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness reference --problem-dir problems/<task_id>` while iterating on `solution/solve.sh` (train/solve + grade with persistent cache under `.alignerr/reference_cache/output`). Use `--skip-solve` to re-grade cached artifacts, `--no-grade` to train only, and `--clean-cache` to wipe the cache.
- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness run --problem-dir problems/<task_id> --runtime ground-truth` before opening a PR; this updates `.alignerr/build_proof.json` with `ground_truth_result`.
- Use `uv run lbx-rl-harness run --problem-dir problems/<task_id> --runtime agent` for optional local DeepAgents runs (requires API keys in `.env.local`).
- A successful ground-truth run creates or overwrites `problems/<task_id>/.alignerr/build_proof.json`; before opening or updating a PR, commit that file with the task.
- If an agent can reason but cannot write `/tmp/output/<artifact>`, check that the task Dockerfile includes `WORKDIR /workdir` and `chown -R 1000:1000 /workdir /tmp/output`.
- The harness auto-loads `.env.local`; never read or print `.env.local` contents.
- Use `--runtime solution` only for deterministic reference-solution scorer checks.
- Inspect `.harness-runs/<run>/trajectory.json` and `verifier/reward-details.json` when debugging failures.
- Keep `.env.local` and `.harness-runs/` out of git.
